@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@orderId = 1
@quoteId = 21
@orderVersion = 7
# Generate ONE new GUID for your own operation. Keep it when investigating a lost response.
# PowerShell: [guid]::NewGuid().ToString()
@requestKey = 5feebfac-a549-41ad-ab35-e8d14e291e03
@csrf = PASTE_CURRENT_SESSION_TOKEN

### Log in as the assigned COLLECTOR using auth-api.http, then fetch a new CSRF token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/csrf

### Read actual version (must be AWAITING_PAYMENT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/collector/orders/{{orderId}}

### Select current ACCEPTED quote; use its id, not versionNumber
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/collector/orders/{{orderId}}/quotes

### Simulated cash payment. No amount/status/actor/timestamps in request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/collector/orders/{{orderId}}/payments/simulate
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{"version":{{orderVersion}},"quoteId":{{quoteId}},"method":"CASH_SIMULATED","requestKey":"{{requestKey}}"}

### Result: COMPLETED, paidAt/completedAt, amount from accepted quote
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/collector/orders/{{orderId}}/payments

### Log in as order owner before using CUSTOMER route
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customer/orders/{{orderId}}/payments

### Log in as ADMIN before using ADMIN route
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/payments

### Alternative on a DIFFERENT eligible order: method TRANSFER_SIMULATED.
# Re-sending for the already completed order always returns 409, including with a new key.
